  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations in Colorado totaled $11.6B in FY2026 to date. Obligations are down 27.9% year over year. The state received 19,386 awards with an average award size of $599K. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $6.3B in obligations, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $1.5B and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $941M. SIERRA NEVADA COMPANY, LLC is the largest vendor with $2B in obligations, followed by LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP at $1.7B and ALLIANCE FOR ENERGY INNOVATION, LLC at $730M. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $1.5B, with Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences next at $1.3B and Engineering Services at $888M. The FY26 total of $11.6B compares with $16.1B in FY25 and a series of prior totals: $15B in FY24, $14.9B in FY23, $14B in FY22, and $12.8B in FY21. These figures are contract obligations and FY2026 totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress.",
    "sections": [
