        "heading": "How did FY2026 federal obligations in Colorado change year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations are down 27.9% year over year. The FY2026 to date total is $11.6B compared with $16.1B in FY25. The downward change reflects the partial nature of FY2026 to date totals and the larger FY2025 total."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate federal contracting in Colorado?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the top buying agency with $6.3B in obligations, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $1.5B and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $941M. SIERRA NEVADA COMPANY, LLC leads vendors with $2B, followed by LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP with $1.7B and ALLIANCE FOR ENERGY INNOVATION, LLC with $730M."
      }
